Triangle read by rows in which the n-th row begins with n and contains at most tau(n) numbers. The r-th term from right is the largest number < n with r divisors, for 1 <= r <= tau(n) skipping any r for which no suitable number exists.

The 87 terms known to OEIS, indexed from `1`.

